<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cornelis Jol</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1597">1597</a>–<a href="/years/1641">1641</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Houtebeen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cornelis Jol, nicknamed Houtebeen ('Peg Leg'), was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> admiral and privateer of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-west-india-company">Dutch West India Company</a>. After years of raiding Spanish and Portuguese shipping in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>, he led the fleet that captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luanda">Luanda</a> from the Portuguese in August 1641 and then took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sao-tome">São Tomé</a>. He died of fever on São Tomé later that year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cornelis-jol.jpg" alt="Cornelis Jol" width="320" height="510" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Spamalot001 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cornelis_%E2%80%9CPegleg%E2%80%9D_Jol.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
